src/KOKKOS/pair_exp6_rx_kokkos.cpp:1138-1151:
  template<int n>
  KOKKOS_INLINE_FUNCTION
  KK_FLOAT __powint(const KK_FLOAT& x, const int)
  {
     static_assert(n == 12, "__powint<> only supports specific integer powers.");
     if (n == 12)
     {
       KK_FLOAT x3 = x*x*x;
       return x3*x3*x3*x3;
     }
  }
Both parts of the finding hold: (a) an identifier beginning with two underscores is reserved to the implementation in every scope (C++ [lex.name]), and this one is at namespace scope in a header-included translation unit; (b) the 'if (n == 12)' is a runtime if, not 'if constexpr', so the function has a path with no return statement -- compilers that do not fold it emit -Wreturn-type and the fall-through is UB if ever taken. The static_assert makes it unreachable in practice, so this is a hygiene issue, not a live bug. Callers are :1373-1420 with n = 12 only.
